        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(line): drop blank entries from trailing commas in agenda/buttons/device directives",
        "body": "## What problem this solves\n\nThe LINE `[[agenda:]]`, `[[buttons:]]`, and `[[device:]]` directive parsers split their comma-separated lists without dropping blank entries. A trailing or doubled comma in agent output — common in LLM output — produces empty model entries:\n\n- **agenda** → an empty-title event → an empty-string Flex `text` component. The LINE Messaging API rejects an empty text with **HTTP 400**, so the whole agenda card is dropped (message loss).\n- **buttons** / **device** → an action whose `label` is empty (also invalid).\n\nThe `[[quick_replies:]]` parser already avoids this by routing its split through the shared `normalizeStringEntries` helper (which trims and drops empties); agenda/buttons/device didn't.\n\nFixes #105380\n\n## What changed\n\n`extensions/line/src/reply-payload-transform.ts`: route the agenda, buttons, and device comma-lists through the existing `normalizeStringEntries` helper (same as `[[quick_replies:]]`), instead of three ad-hoc trim/filter pipelines. One canonical normalization path, no drift.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### 1. Real LINE API — the actual directive-generated payload\n\n`parseLineDirectives(\"[[agenda: Today | Standup:9am, Lunch:12pm,]]\")` output posted to the LINE `validate/push` endpoint (validates a payload without sending; token/recipient redacted):\n\n**Before (current `main`):**\n```\naltText: 📋 Today (3 events)\nHTTP 400 - {\"message\":\"A message (messages[0]) in the request body is invalid\",\n  \"details\":[{\"message\":\"must be non-empty text\",\n  \"property\":\"/body/contents/2/contents/2/contents/2/contents/0/text\"}]}\n```\n\n**After (this PR):**\n```\naltText: 📋 Today (2 events)\nHTTP 200 - {}\n```\n\nThe 400 points at the empty `text` component deep inside the real agenda card; after the fix the generated payload validates.\n\n### 2. Source-level reproduction (`parseLineDirectives`, current `main`)\n\n| directive (trailing/doubled comma) | before | after |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `[[agenda: Today \\| Standup:9am, Lunch:12pm,]]` | 3 events, 1 empty `text` component | 2 events, 0 |\n| `[[buttons: Menu \\| Choose \\| Opt1:d1, Opt2:d2,]]` | 3 actions, 1 empty label | 2 actions, 0 |\n| `[[device: TV \\| Box \\| Playing \\| Play:toggle,, Menu:menu]]` | 1 empty action label | 0 |\n\n### 3. Tests\n\nNew regression tests in `reply-payload-transform.test.ts` (trailing-comma agenda/buttons, doubled-comma device). Verified red on `main`, green with the fix:\n\n```\n# without fix (origin/main parser):\n × drops trailing commas in agenda events   → expected '📋 Today (3 events)' to be '📋 Today (2 events)'\n × drops trailing commas in buttons actions  → expected length 2 but got 3\n × drops doubled commas in device controls   → expected [Array(6)] to not include ''\n Tests  3 failed | 12 passed (15)\n\n# with fix:\n Tests  15 passed (15)\n```\n\nTypecheck (`tsgo -b tsconfig.extensions.projects.json`) clean.\n",
        "branch": "fix/line-directive-empty-entries",
